One directory per uTLS fingerprint name the core takes from a capture: hello.hex (the first TLS record the client
sent), SOURCE (which client, on what, when, from which run of niko's browser-hellos.yml) and SHUFFLE (yes: two
captures in a row sent the extensions in different orders, so the core shuffles them per connection too). The files
come from the run's "hellos-*" artifacts, as they are.
